  id: arg-51b5083a44
  target: arg-9255ccd089
  target_statement: A federal “national holiday” designation does not automatically create the paid, usable time the target relies on.
A national Election Day holiday should be enacted as a concrete voting-access reform, not as a calendar change alone. If Congress designates Election Day a national holiday, the statute can also include an enforceable federal guarantee of protected time to vote (e.g., paid time off or a federally required voting-leave right). With that built into the policy, the key problem raised by the attack—workers having no usable time and losing wages—would be addressed by law, not left to whether private employers voluntarily accommodate a holiday.

